1
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:28,500
Royal Matchmaker is a romance, tv movie film directed by Mike Rohl.

2
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
A struggling NYC matchmaker is hired by a king to find his son a
suitable wife in time for a national celebration.

3
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:13,500
As the clock ticks towards her deadline, the matchmaker finds him the perfect
wife -- only to realize that she’s fallen in love with him!

4
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Kate Gleason, played by Bethany Joy Lenz.

5
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:58,500
Prince Sebastian, played by Will Kemp.

6
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Britney Van Howell, played by Brittany Bristow.

7
00:37:37,500 --> 00:37:43,500
Countess Petra Petrovich, played by Elva Trill.

8
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
King Edward, played by Simon Dutton.

9
00:48:22,500 --> 00:48:28,500
Loraine Paisley, played by Poppy Roe.

10
00:53:45,000 --> 00:53:51,000
The Princess and the Matchmaker (Korean: 궁합) is a 2018 South Korean
period romantic comedy film directed by Hong Chang-pyo.

11
00:59:07,500 --> 00:59:13,500
The film stars Shim Eun-kyung, Lee Seung-gi, Kim Sang-kyung, Yeon
Woo-jin, Kang Min-hyuk, Choi Woo-shik and Jo Bok-rae.

12
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
The film tells story of a saju expert, Seo Do-yoon, who received an order from the King to help
him pick a husband for his daughter, Princess Song-hwa, based on their fortune.

13
01:09:52,500 --> 01:09:58,500
It is the second installment of Jupiter Film's three-part film project on the Korean fortune-telling traditions,
following The Face Reader which was released in 2013 and followed by Feng Shui later in 2018.

14
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:21,000
The film explores themes of prince, royalty, matchmaker, hallmark.

15
01:20:37,500 --> 01:20:43,500
The tone is emotional.
